{
  "summary": "This experiment swapped the RNA encoder from scvi_n200 to scgpt while holding the multiprofile + avgpool RNA-only configuration constant (the single-variable change from the current best, config_004), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.530 and F1 of 0.515 versus 0.650 and 0.628 for scvi_n200 in the identical multiprofile avgpool setting. Because only the encoder was changed, the ~12-point accuracy drop is cleanly attributable to the encoder choice, indicating that scvi_n200 is the substantially superior RNA encoder for this classification task and that the ~0.65 accuracy ceiling observed with scvi_n200 is not an artifact of the encoder. It remains uncertain whether scgpt could perform differently under alternative aggregation strategies or in a multimodal fusion context, and whether the remaining headroom above 0.65 lies in the fusion axis or in further tuning of the scvi_n200 pipeline."
}

